From: Vladimir Skvortsov <vskvortsov@emcraft.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:33:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] torizon: boot only from UFS when hardened

The distro boot scan tries USB before UFS. A hardened U-Boot denies
"usb start" on a closed device, and a signed image has no reason to
look for a boot script on a USB drive, so leave USB out of the boot
targets when the Toradex hardening is built in.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Vladimir Skvortsov <vskvortsov@emcraft.com>
---
 include/configs/lec_mtk_i1200.h | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/configs/lec_mtk_i1200.h b/include/configs/lec_mtk_i1200.h
index 0d9dd73c..0e523676 100755
--- a/include/configs/lec_mtk_i1200.h
+++ b/include/configs/lec_mtk_i1200.h
@@ -85,7 +85,8 @@
 #define BOOT_TARGET_MMC(func)
 #endif
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_CMD_USB
+/* A hardened (signed) build boots from the on-module UFS only. */
+#if defined(CONFIG_CMD_USB) && !defined(CONFIG_TDX_SECBOOT_HARDENING)
 #define BOOT_TARGET_USB(func) func(USB, usb, 0)
 #else
 #define BOOT_TARGET_USB(func)
-- 
2.25.1

